                "The Black Hole incident occurred on the night of June 20, 1756: British survivor J.Z. Holwell claimed 146 European prisoners were crammed into a tiny dungeon (18 × 14 feet 10 inches), resulting in 123 deaths from suffocation and heat exhaustion.",
                "Siraj renamed Calcutta 'Alinagar' (in honor of his grandfather Alivardi) and placed the city under the custody of officer Manik Chand.",
