                "In return for his installation, Mir Qasim ceded the fertile districts of Burdwan, Midnapore, and Chittagong to the East India Company.",
                "Mir Qasim proved to be the most capable and independent-minded Nawab of Bengal: he shifted his capital from Murshidabad to Munger (Bihar) in 1762 to escape British surveillance.",
                "At Munger, Mir Qasim established a modern foundry for casting cannons and manufacturing flintlock muskets, hired European drillmasters (like Walter Reinhard / Sumroo), and reorganized revenue collection."
