                "Haidar Ali (born c. 1721) rose from an ordinary horseman (faujdar of Dindigul 1755) to seize de facto sovereignty of Mysore in 1761, ousting Nanjaraj.",
                "At Dindigul, Haidar Ali established a modern French-assisted artillery arsenal and drilled his troops in Western military tactics.",
                "First Anglo-Mysore War (1767–1769): British formed a Triple Alliance with the Nizam of Hyderabad and the Marathas against Haidar Ali.",
                "Haidar Ali broke the alliance through brilliant diplomacy (paying off the Marathas and winning over the Nizam), marched across the Carnatic, and appeared before the gates of Madras in 1769, dictating the Treaty of Madras."
